The problem is that the elseif statements are not correctly written. In MATLAB, the condition for elseif must be written as two separate conditions connected by "&&" (logical AND). The correct way to write the elseif statements is as follows:

```
elseif x>=-1 && x<=1
y=-5.*x+10;
elseif x>=1 && x<=3
y=-10.*x.^2+35.*x-20;
elseif x>=3 && x<=4
y=-5.*x+10;
elseif x>=4 && x<=5
y=-10;
```

This ensures that MATLAB correctly evaluates the conditions for each elseif statement. With this correction, your function file should work as expected.

Here is a simple batch script that should do the trick:

@echo off
set source="c:\fubar1\"
set destination="c:\fubar2\"

for /f "tokens=*" %%a in ('dir /b /a-d %source%\*.txt') do (
    set filename=%%a
    if not "%%a"=="%filename%" (
        copy "%%a" "%destination%\%%a"
    )
)

This script will copy all .txt files from the source folder to the destination folder, but it will not copy the file if it already exists in the destination folder. If you want to overwrite existing files, remove the "if not" line.

Just replace "c:\fubar1\" and "c:\fubar2\" with your actual source and destination paths. Also, make sure to save the script with a .bat extension.

