The savedelimiter option is used to store the environment name in the macro \tcb@savedelimiter. This macro is used in the tabularx hack to set the correct environment name. If this name is not set correctly, the tabularx hack fails.


The solution is to use the savedelimiter option in the outer box and to set the correct environment name:


\newtcolorbox{testbox}[1][]{
  width=.5\textwidth,
  savedelimiter={\tcb@savedelimiter\testbox},
  #1
}


Then the tabularx hack works in the inner box:


\begin{testbox}
  \begin{tcolorbox}[tabularx={l},width=4cm]
    test1 \\\hline
    test2
  \end{tcolorbox}
